WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:03.520
- Today we're going to talk
about the best buys under $50

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:07.050
to make your life in law school
just a little bit better.

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:11.490
This is a companion video to
the expensive, nice to have,

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:15.080
but not necessarily necessary
purchases in law school.

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:17.760
This are the things that
really punch above their weight

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:19.610
you can get pennies on the dollar.

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:21.580
So stick around and learn how you can make

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:24.457
your life in law school
just a little bit better.

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:27.290
(fun theme music)

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:32.660
Okay, so the first cheap
product that I would recommend

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:34.910
is this humble bookstand.

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:37.050
It weighs only about an ounce.

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:37.883
It folds up.

00:00:37.883 --> 00:00:38.920
You can put it in your backpack.

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:39.800
You can carry it around.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:41.990
You can travel with it almost anywhere.

00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:44.323
And the reason is because you can't avoid

00:00:44.323 --> 00:00:45.960
reading your case book.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:48.790
Even if you use our methods
and limit the amount

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:50.740
of case book reading you're going to do,

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:53.170
you still going to have to
read out of your case book

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:55.690
every once in awhile and that's okay.

00:00:55.690 --> 00:00:58.600
But because you're going
to be spending so much time

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:01.440
reading out of a huge, heavy case book,

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:04.820
this little foldable
bookstand is invaluable.

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:07.570
The way that it works
is you just unfold it.

00:01:07.570 --> 00:01:09.950
You take your case book.

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:11.800
You slide it in.

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:14.080
And then you extend it out a little bit,

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:16.810
which is hard to do while I'm
actually carrying the thing.

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:18.180
But you sort of get the idea

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:20.490
that you can put it on your desk.

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:22.320
Read out of the book while working

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:25.180
on a laptop or iPad or taking notes.

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:27.440
Then you don't have to crane your neck

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:29.490
while looking at the
book while it's vertical.

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:32.320
It's at a 45 degree angle
and you can take it anywhere.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:34.400
You can take it to the library.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:37.340
You can take it into a friend's apartment

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:39.170
when you're studying together.

00:01:39.170 --> 00:01:41.240
You can do just about anything.

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:45.850
And for $15 on Amazon,
I wouldn't go anywhere

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:47.150
in law school without this thing.

00:01:47.150 --> 00:01:48.530
You'll use it for hours.

00:01:48.530 --> 00:01:49.420
It's really cheap.

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:52.250
I've seen a bunch of
law students on YouTube

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:53.240
talking about this thing.

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:55.160
I used it when I went to law school.

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:58.890
And I recommend anyone who
is either going to law school

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:02.010
or in law school get one of
these things and save your back.

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:04.370
By the way, you can find
links to all of these products

00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:06.440
in the description below.

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:09.450
So I recommend getting
one of these bookstands.

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:10.570
It will help save your neck.

00:02:10.570 --> 00:02:11.680
It will help save your back.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:13.380
And it will just make
reading your case book

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:15.122
just a little bit more pleasant,

00:02:15.122 --> 00:02:18.194
which when you're reading these cases,

00:02:18.194 --> 00:02:19.940
anything you can do to make your life

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:22.490
a little bit more pleasant
is probably worthwhile.

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:23.860
So the next thing I recommend

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:27.150
is getting either a white
board and dry erase markers

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:28.390
or some butcher paper.

00:02:28.390 --> 00:02:31.890
You need something to help
diagram the law itself.

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:33.410
The law is complicated.

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:36.310
And when you get to issues
spotting hypothetical,

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:38.930
it sort of flows like a decision tree.

00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:40.750
You have the causes of action.

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:43.220
The elements under the causes of action.

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:46.380
The definition of the
elements, sub-elements.

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:49.570
And you need to see how
that all flows together.

00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:54.570
And diagraming, usually
on a wall with markers,

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:58.900
really helps to understand
how things fit together.

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:01.480
I think everyone is familiar
with a dry erase board

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:04.340
or you can even use a chalk board.

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:06.240
But I prefer butcher paper.

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:09.320
Butcher paper is great
because you can use any marker

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:12.930
and save on expensive white
board dry erase markers.

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:15.800
The best part though is
you can save it for later.

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:18.840
One roll can last your entire semester.

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:21.480
You can also just buy a
bunch of dry erase markers

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:23.920
and write on the window,
a beautiful nine style.

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:28.030
As long as you're willing to
look like an insane person

00:03:28.030 --> 00:03:32.340
while you are writing on the
window with dry erase markers.

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:34.510
Of course, I've done crazier things

00:03:34.510 --> 00:03:35.610
to save money in law school.

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:36.840
So I wouldn't blame you.

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:39.700
Okay, the next thing I
recommend in law school

00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:40.940
are some ear plugs.

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:42.420
Now I think everyone's familiar

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:45.280
with these little form things
that you put in your ear.

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:47.740
But ear plugs have a couple of advantages

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:49.760
in law school in particular

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:52.150
that might not be obvious on first glance.

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:55.480
In law school a big problem
that almost everyone has

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:57.340
is getting enough sleep.

00:03:57.340 --> 00:03:59.870
Ear plugs can really
help when your neighbor

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:02.868
decides to hold an impromptu
band rehearsal at midnight.

00:04:02.868 --> 00:04:03.701
(folk music)

00:04:03.701 --> 00:04:05.390
Or if your roommates have a very different

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:06.850
sleep pattern than you,

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:09.596
Or if you just live on a busy street.

00:04:09.596 --> 00:04:13.310
Ear plugs, if you use them consistently,

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:16.280
can help you create a
consistent sleep pattern.

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:18.290
It isn't interrupted
if there happens to be

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:20.570
stuff going on that particular night.

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:22.700
It takes some time to get used to them.

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:23.970
So I would recommend using them

00:04:23.970 --> 00:04:26.420
even when there aren't
loud noises going on

00:04:26.420 --> 00:04:28.170
and times of emergency.

00:04:28.170 --> 00:04:30.230
I would just get in the
habit of using them.

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:32.690
You can get good sleep every night.

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:37.140
Also, ear plugs can help
you create consistency

00:04:37.140 --> 00:04:39.000
in your practice test.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.310
Now, we have a number
of videos to talk about

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:44.320
how practice tests are one
of the most important things

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:46.200
you can do to increase your chances

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:48.150
of getting a better grade in law school.

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:49.929
And just see the link below.

00:04:49.929 --> 00:04:54.620
But one of the problem of
doing practice tests at home

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:59.030
is that it's very different
from taking an exam in class.

00:04:59.030 --> 00:05:03.890
When you take a law school exam
in class during the finals,

00:05:03.890 --> 00:05:08.380
the sound of clacking keyboards
is absolutely deafing.

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:10.350
And then there are other
people that will be coughing.

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:11.490
They'll be rustling bags.

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:13.240
They'll be getting in their backpacks.

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:17.400
All of these noises and
sounds will not be present

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:19.040
when you're taking your practice test.

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:20.590
You'll probably be
taking your practice test

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:23.810
at home under ideal conditions.

00:05:23.810 --> 00:05:27.750
Which is fine, but you
don't want to get used to

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:31.450
taking practice tests under
absolutely ideal conditions.

00:05:31.450 --> 00:05:33.840
If you go into the final
with ear plugs though,

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:37.090
you reduce some of that
sound and is more similar

00:05:37.090 --> 00:05:40.100
to the way you practice tests at home.

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:43.390
And as sort of plamonian response,

00:05:43.390 --> 00:05:48.390
you can associate ear plugs
with going into test mode.

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:52.040
The second that you put
ear plugs into your ears,

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:54.820
your mind will think,
okay, this is test time.

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:56.870
Now it's time to pull out all the stops.

00:05:56.870 --> 00:05:58.730
And you'll be in the
mental state necessary

00:05:58.730 --> 00:06:00.020
to crush the exam.

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:02.480
The next cheap thing that I
would recommend in law school

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:04.060
is a physical calendar.

00:06:04.060 --> 00:06:07.240
Not a digital calendar
like in Outlook or Gmail,

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:11.040
but an actual paper, physical calendar.

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:12.700
These things are invaluable.

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:14.780
There is not enough time in your semester

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:16.910
as it first appears.

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:19.400
What starts out as eight to 10 weeks,

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:21.240
it seems like an eternity,

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:23.710
but that will go by so fast.

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:27.220
And you need to be able to
see where you are in time.

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:29.580
How much time is left so you can make sure

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:31.010
you finish your outline.

00:06:31.010 --> 00:06:33.570
You can make sure you
start doing practice tests

00:06:33.570 --> 00:06:34.830
as early as possible.

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:38.300
And that you are ready by the
time that finals come around.

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:40.020
And a physical calendar helps you

00:06:40.020 --> 00:06:41.760
see in a glance where you are.

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:44.530
Are you falling behind
and chances are, yes.

00:06:44.530 --> 00:06:47.928
And the sooner you realize
that you simply don't have time

00:06:47.928 --> 00:06:50.985
to do these insane, multi-page,

00:06:50.985 --> 00:06:54.220
rainbow style of case briefs the better.

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:56.630
You need to genesis
that as soon as possible

00:06:56.630 --> 00:06:58.930
because there just isn't
enough time in a semester

00:06:58.930 --> 00:07:02.070
to do all of that unnecessary work.

00:07:02.070 --> 00:07:04.210
And a physical calendar will show you

00:07:04.210 --> 00:07:08.075
where you are in time and
help you plan everything out.

00:07:08.075 --> 00:07:10.718
Better to do it sooner rather than later.

00:07:10.718 --> 00:07:13.960
Getting a physical calendar
will save so much time

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:16.850
and anguish and really help
you plan out your semester.

00:07:16.850 --> 00:07:20.690
Okay, so, the last relatively
inexpensive product

00:07:20.690 --> 00:07:24.350
that I would recommend for
law school is an alarm.

00:07:24.350 --> 00:07:27.970
I know that sounds crazy,
but get a separate alarm.

00:07:27.970 --> 00:07:29.300
Do not use your phone.

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:33.120
Do not let your cellphone
reside anywhere near your bed.

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:36.589
Now, I keep my cellphone
outside my bedroom.

00:07:36.589 --> 00:07:39.620
It used to be that I would get work emails

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:41.440
all throughout the night.

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:45.470
And in a plamonian response,
I would pick up the cellphone,

00:07:45.470 --> 00:07:49.150
interrupt my sleep and look at the email.

00:07:49.150 --> 00:07:52.210
But the truth is whether
you're in law practice

00:07:52.210 --> 00:07:54.180
or if you're in law school,

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:56.690
the emails that come in at
two o'clock in the morning,

00:07:56.690 --> 00:07:57.960
are just not that important.

00:07:57.960 --> 00:07:59.910
They can wait until the next day.

00:07:59.910 --> 00:08:02.270
So what I recommend and
this is a little bit

00:08:02.270 --> 00:08:04.337
on the pricey side but you
can get cheaper options,

00:08:04.337 --> 00:08:06.007
is a sunrise alarm.

00:08:06.007 --> 00:08:07.786
These things are great.

00:08:07.786 --> 00:08:09.720
Unlike a traditional alarm

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:12.167
that just has a blaring
sound to wake you up,

00:08:12.167 --> 00:08:16.460
this displays light gradually coming on

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:20.520
like a dimmer, a reverse
dimmer to convince your body

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:24.860
that it's sunrise and that
you should get up gradually

00:08:24.860 --> 00:08:25.960
as the sun rises.

00:08:25.960 --> 00:08:28.800
And this works even when
it's pitch black outside.

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:30.600
There's sounds that go along with it.

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:34.450
This is a much less jarring
way to wake yourself up.

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:37.650
And I am so much more
rested when I wake up

00:08:37.650 --> 00:08:41.310
with a sunrise alarm as
compared to a blaring sound.

00:08:41.310 --> 00:08:43.080
And I got a better night sleep

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:47.680
because I separated my cellphone
from the alarm function.

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:51.990
There is a great video
on YouTube of Simon Sinek

00:08:51.990 --> 00:08:54.510
where he talks about the dumbest thing

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:57.290
that the millennial generations
does, myself included.

00:08:57.290 --> 00:09:01.670
It used to be was using
their cellphones as an alarm

00:09:01.670 --> 00:09:05.070
and being too cheap to buy
a separate physical alarm.

00:09:05.070 --> 00:09:06.787
I whole heartily agree with him.

00:09:06.787 --> 00:09:10.220
Just get some other clock radio

00:09:10.220 --> 00:09:11.270
if you want to go the cheap route,

00:09:11.270 --> 00:09:13.430
or if you want to spent
a little bit more money,

00:09:13.430 --> 00:09:18.430
you can get any number of
$30 to $100 sunrise alarms.

00:09:18.946 --> 00:09:21.016
They all seem to work pretty well.

00:09:21.016 --> 00:09:24.920
A separate alarm will allow
you to get more sleep.

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:27.590
It will wake you up more gradually.

00:09:27.590 --> 00:09:29.050
You'll be in a better mood.

00:09:29.050 --> 00:09:31.680
You'll be more alert for
your law school classes

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:32.513
throughout the day.

00:09:32.513 --> 00:09:35.080
Studies show that a lack of
sleep prevents the ability

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:38.050
to memorize, internalize
information and remember.

00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:41.230
So just an hour of sleep
more per night alone

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:43.507
could put you above your
classmates in law school.

00:09:43.507 --> 00:09:48.070
So law school is all about
creating a competitive advantage

00:09:48.070 --> 00:09:50.150
as compared to your classmates.

00:09:50.150 --> 00:09:53.160
These little things, whether
it's a foldable bookstand

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:56.160
so you save your neck from neck pain,

00:09:56.160 --> 00:09:59.030
and allow yourself to
study a little bit longer

00:09:59.030 --> 00:10:03.280
every day in the library or
a separate physical alarm

00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:06.619
to get more sleep at night
and to wake up more alert.

00:10:06.619 --> 00:10:11.330
These things may not be huge
advantages in of themselves,

00:10:11.330 --> 00:10:15.190
but they compound over
time and allow you to study

00:10:15.190 --> 00:10:17.499
a little bit longer, be more alert

00:10:17.499 --> 00:10:20.130
and just be a better
law student all around.

00:10:20.130 --> 00:10:21.550
And when you're graded on a curve,

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:23.130
as you are in law school,

00:10:23.130 --> 00:10:24.920
these little things add up

00:10:24.920 --> 00:10:27.990
and allow you to get an
advantage over your classmates.

00:10:27.990 --> 00:10:30.300
And that's what Legal Eagle is all about.

